 ("p", "The Equator divides the Earth into the **Northern and Southern Hemispheres**. The Prime Meridian (with 180°) divides it into the **Eastern and Western Hemispheres**. India lies in the Northern and Eastern Hemispheres, roughly between **8°N and 37°N** and between **68°E and 97°E**."),
